    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Local test workflow \u2014 setup\n\n**1) File location (important in n8n 2.x)**\nSince n8n 2.0 the file nodes can only read/write inside `~/.n8n-files`\n(Docker: `/home/node/.n8n-files`). So:\n- Put your dashboard HTML there, e.g. `/home/node/.n8n-files/dashboard.html`\n- The Excel output lands there too, e.g. `/home/node/.n8n-files/tvm-overdue.xlsx`\n\nTo use another folder, set `N8N_RESTRICT_FILE_ACCESS_TO=/your/dir` (semicolon-separated\nfor several) and restart n8n.\n- Docker: mount a host folder in, e.g. `-v /host/tvm:/home/node/.n8n-files`, then drop the\n  HTML in and collect the xlsx from the host side.\n- Windows (npm install): the path looks like `C:\\\\Users\\\\<you>\\\\.n8n-files\\\\dashboard.html`.\n\n**2) Config node**\n- `inputHtmlPath` / `outputXlsxPath` \u2014 point at your files inside the allowed dir\n- `ownerList` \u2014 your 5 owners (prefilled)\n\n**3) Run it**\nClick **Execute workflow** (manual trigger). It reads the HTML, keeps Overdue rows for the\nowner list, and writes the xlsx (creating it, or overwriting if it already exists).\n\n**Notes**\n- Columns: Overdue Tickets, Ticket URL, Severity, Assignment, State, Summary.\n  Ticket + URL are plain text here; a clickable `=HYPERLINK` needs the online/Graph version.\n- Regenerates the whole file each run (same full-sync behaviour). For a true incremental\n  merge (read the existing xlsx, upsert, write back) ask and I'll add it.\n- The \"Extract fields\" selectors match the dashboard's current column order.\n",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "30ad2da0-a38d-4715-980f-55d480197942",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        560
      ]
    }
  ],
